/* ================= world entrance art on the map (Oct 2026) =================
   Each world can have its own drawn entrance instead of an emoji, tied to its kind of math. The core map (index.html, the gate drawing in
   wFrame) draws MQ_GATE_ART[world] when its picture has loaded, bottom-aligned on the gate tile, w tiles wide, and keeps the emoji until
   then (and for worlds without art). A locked world shows its art faded with a 🔒 on it.
   haunt is drawn 4 tiles wide (not 2.6) so it is as tall as the Number Town building it stands next to.
   caves: the Subtraction Caves' Cave Mouth (the owner picked it from 4 mockups): a rocky hill, a stone archway whose keystone carries the
   minus sign, the inside drawn as darker and darker grey bands so it goes down into the hill, crystals and grass by the door.
   forest: the Addition Forest's Treehouse (the owner's idea): a big leafy tree, a red-roofed house on a platform with lit windows, its door
   darker and darker inside like the cave, a round plaque with the plus sign over it, a ladder, a toadstool and grass.
   castle: the Division Castle's gatehouse: lavender stone (to stand out on the purple ground), two towers with purple roofs and flags,
   battlements, a stone-framed gate darker and darker inside, and a round shield with the division sign over it.
   volcano: the Multiplication Volcano: a charcoal mountain (to stand out on the red ground) with a glowing crater, smoke and two lava
   streams, a doorway at its foot going from deep red to black, and a round plaque with the times sign over it. */
